Fri Oct 23 07:14:42 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.12.0 (upstream tag v0.12.0, 2026-10-23):
  * 0.9.0 was an untagged version bump only
  * Security hardening (0.12.0): the local control server needs a
    per-session token (CWE-306); atomic writes via an exclusive
    temp file (CWE-59); bounded work/allocation in geometry,
    constraints, rendering, DXF/SVG/PDF import, fonts, MTEXT and
    Lisp (CWE-400/407/789); XATTACH paths submitted as literal
    text (CWE-74); craft-fonts manifest paths confined (CWE-22)
  * New commands: BURST, BREAKLINE, TXT2MTXT, MOCORO, SHAPES,
    ALIASEDIT dialog, AUDITCTL with .adt logs; HATCHEDIT adds and
    removes boundary loops; selection cycling (Shift+Space)
  * DWG/DXF interop: justified text, DIMPOST, second-layout
    entities, millimetre layouts, plot window corners, ACAD_TABLE
    blocks, current text style handle, foreign handles above 2^48,
    orphaned DGN line styles left out so bloated files open
  * Editing fixes: ARC Ctrl direction, BREAK on closed polylines
    and Z kept, JOIN cLose, Shift ortho override, constraint and
    dynamic-block grip fixes, multileader sizes, ID/DIST/LIST Z
  * Interface: Hungarian, Turkish and Greek translations, interface
    scale and two-click selection options, menu bar hover switch
  * cadcraft-cli: --help exits 0; image export warns about
    entities it cannot draw
  * No CVE keywords in the 0.8.0-0.12.0 range; cargo_vendor audit
    clean ("All lockfiles are audited", no RUSTSEC advisories).
- Re-vendored at upstream's locked versions (update=false kept):
  the only new crate is chrono 0.4.45 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), so the
  vendor-tree licence set and License tag are unchanged; craft-libs
  git revs unchanged; no new system deps; cargo floor 1.95 still
- Set the fixed metainfo release date to 2026-10-23 (v0.12.0)
- Legal-Review-Notice: correct the acadrust version to 0.6.4 (the
  locked version since 0.7.0)

